  "note": "Hybrid WebGPU C2C query preparation: streaming exact f64 coordinates with each batch versus staging each lane's exact query snapshot once per job in WASM. Both controls use identical cached reference snapshots, verification worker count, GPU batch size, prefetch, bounds, SIMD, workgroup and adaptive-summary controls. CPU pool prewarming, file loading and initial reference setup are excluded. Five warm-up pairs precede ten (or requested) alternating timed pairs. Staged coordinates are not reused across jobs: every timed call includes packing, query transfers, WASM ownership, GPU readbacks, verification, ordered joining, query release submission and exact summaries. Coordinates retain original f64 bits; each source query is staged to one lane only. The total coordinate bytes are unchanged; allocation/copy scheduling and per-batch payloads differ. Every pair must match displayed f32 distance bits, exact reported f64 statistics and certificate counts. Timed worker/GPU fallback is rejected. Preparation can overlap the first GPU dispatch, and gpuMillis includes overlapping verification; phase intervals must not be summed. CPU/GPU clocks, power and other applications are uncontrolled; no cross-machine speed guarantee. Input hashes and provenance are recorded for supplied files."
